Text:
This design is about which folders of a desk are 'well shaped'.
A Zip models what a zip file holds.
A Segment is a sequence of 'units'.
Desk.time(File) and Desk.time(Id) have no Notation: each desk defines them.
//later: Fix moves away an entry whose name, after Fix gives that entry a valid name, is longer than 191 characters before its extension.
//later: a name that Fix gives to an entry starts with "_" only when the old name of that entry starts with "_".
//later: Fix ends with an error when Fix leaves the Fearless project with no entry: such a Fearless project can not be repaired.
//later: Fix changes nothing inside a hidden folder. When an entry inside a hidden folder is not ok, Fix moves the whole hidden folder out of the Fearless project, in one move: the outermost folder with a hidden name that holds that entry.
//later: Fix moves nothing out of a zip file. When the changes that Fix makes inside a zip file can not make that zip file ok, Fix leaves the content of that zip file as it is and moves the whole zip file out of the Fearless project, in one move: the outermost zip file, for a zip file inside a zip file.

Grammar:
Zip ::= "Zip{" ZipEntries "}"
ZipEntries ::= ZipEntry1 .. ZipEntryn
ZipEntry ::= Segment "->" Zip | Segment "->" File
Thing ::= Element | Zip
ThingEntries ::= ThingEntry1 .. ThingEntryn
ThingEntry ::= Segment "->" Thing
Visibility ::= "visible" | "hidden"
Nat ::= [0-9]+

Notation: fearlessProject.text(Desk, Segment) = AnyText where:
- each unit of Segment is a number from 32 to 126
- AnyText has one character for each unit of Segment, in the same order: the ASCII character with the number of that unit

Notation: fearlessProject.len(Desk, Segment) = Nat where:
- Nat is the number of units of Segment

Notation: fearlessProject.isHidden(Desk, Segment) where:
- the first unit of Segment is the unit of "."

Notation: fearlessProject.isZip(Desk, Segment) where:
- the last four units of Segment are the units of ".zip"

Notation: fearlessProject.isZipOf(Desk, Segment, Segment') where:
- Segment is the units of Segment' followed by the units of ".zip"

Notation: fearlessProject.folderNameOk(Desk, Segment) where:
- fearlessProject.text(Desk, Segment) is of form SegmentBase

Notation: fearlessProject.fileNameOk(Desk, Segment) where:
- fearlessProject.text(Desk, Segment) is of form SegmentBase "." OSExtension, or of form SegmentBase "." MultiExtension

Notation: fearlessProject.hiddenNameOk(Desk, Segment) where:
- fearlessProject.text(Desk, Segment) = AnyText
- AnyText does not end with "." or " "
- AnyText holds none of "<", ">", ":", "\"", "/", "\\", "|", "?", "*"
- the part of AnyText before the first ".", without its ending spaces, with "A" to "Z" turned into "a" to "z", is not of form ReservedName, and is not "conin$" or "conout$"

Notation: fearlessProject.okTogether(Desk, Segment, Segment') where:
- fearlessProject.text(Desk, Segment) is undefined, or fearlessProject.text(Desk, Segment') is undefined, or fearlessProject.text(Desk, Segment) and fearlessProject.text(Desk, Segment') are not equal after "A" to "Z" are turned into "a" to "z"

Notation: fearlessProject.timeOk(Desk, File) where:
- Desk.time(File) is at most 5 seconds after the current time

Notation: fearlessProject.timeOk(Desk, Id) where:
- Desk.time(Id) is at most 5 seconds after the current time

Notation: fearlessProject.timeOk(Desk, Zip)

Signature: fearlessProject.names(Desk, Thing) = ThingEntries

Notation: fearlessProject.names(Desk, Id) = Entries where:
- Desk = Ids ";" Folders Id "{" Entries "}" Folders'

Notation: fearlessProject.names(Desk, "Zip{" ZipEntries "}") = ZipEntries

Notation: fearlessProject.wellShaped(Desk, DeskPath) where:
- Desk.at(DeskPath) = Id
- Id is not one of the 'root ids' of Desk
- fearlessProject.timeOk(Desk, Id)
- fearlessProject.names(Desk, Id) is not empty
- fearlessProject.ok(Desk, fearlessProject.names(Desk, Id), "visible", 0, 0)

Signature: fearlessProject.ok(Desk, ThingEntries, Visibility, Nat, Nat')

Notation: fearlessProject.ok(Desk, Segment1 "->" Thing1 .. Segmentn "->" Thingn, Visibility, Nat, Nat') where:
- for each i, j in 1..n with i != j: fearlessProject.okTogether(Desk, Segmenti, Segmentj)
- if Visibility is "visible": for each i, j in 1..n where not fearlessProject.isHidden(Desk, Segmenti): not fearlessProject.isZipOf(Desk, Segmenti, Segmentj)
- for each i in 1..n: fearlessProject.okEntry(Desk, Segmenti, Thingi, Visibility, Nat + fearlessProject.len(Desk, Segmenti), Nat')

Signature: fearlessProject.okEntry(Desk, Segment, Thing, Visibility, Nat, Nat')

Notation: fearlessProject.okEntry(Desk, Segment, Thing, "visible", Nat, Nat') where:
- not fearlessProject.isHidden(Desk, Segment)
- Nat <= 200
- Thing is of form Zip, or Thing is of form Id and Thing is not one of the 'root ids' of Desk
- fearlessProject.folderNameOk(Desk, Segment)
- fearlessProject.timeOk(Desk, Thing)
- fearlessProject.names(Desk, Thing) is not empty
- fearlessProject.ok(Desk, fearlessProject.names(Desk, Thing), "visible", Nat + 1, Nat')

Notation: fearlessProject.okEntry(Desk, Segment, File, "visible", Nat, Nat') where:
- not fearlessProject.isHidden(Desk, Segment)
- Nat <= 200
- fearlessProject.fileNameOk(Desk, Segment)
- fearlessProject.timeOk(Desk, File)
- not fearlessProject.isZip(Desk, Segment)

Notation: fearlessProject.okEntry(Desk, Segment, File, "visible", Nat, Nat') where:
- not fearlessProject.isHidden(Desk, Segment)
- Nat <= 200
- fearlessProject.fileNameOk(Desk, Segment)
- fearlessProject.timeOk(Desk, File)
- fearlessProject.isZip(Desk, Segment)
- Nat' <= 64
- fearlessProject.zip(Desk, File) = Zip
- fearlessProject.names(Desk, Zip) is not empty
- fearlessProject.ok(Desk, fearlessProject.names(Desk, Zip), "visible", Nat - 3, Nat' + 1)

Notation: fearlessProject.okEntry(Desk, Segment, File, Visibility, Nat, Nat') where:
- Nat' is 0
- Visibility is "hidden" or fearlessProject.isHidden(Desk, Segment)
- Nat <= 250
- fearlessProject.hiddenNameOk(Desk, Segment)

Notation: fearlessProject.okEntry(Desk, Segment, Thing, Visibility, Nat, Nat') where:
- Nat' is 0
- Visibility is "hidden" or fearlessProject.isHidden(Desk, Segment)
- Nat <= 250
- Thing is of form Zip, or Thing is of form Id and Thing is not one of the 'root ids' of Desk
- fearlessProject.hiddenNameOk(Desk, Segment)
- if Visibility is "visible": fearlessProject.names(Desk, Thing) is not empty
- fearlessProject.ok(Desk, fearlessProject.names(Desk, Thing), "hidden", Nat + 1, Nat')

Notation: fearlessProject.zip(Desk, File) = Zip where:
- File has at most 2147483639 bytes
- every way of reading File used by a widely used tool gives the same tree: the same names, the same content
- the content of each entry of File has at most 2147483639 bytes
- AnyText1 .. AnyTextn are the names of the entries of File, in the order of the entries
- for each entry of File, the time of that entry is at most one day after the current time
- no two of AnyText1 .. AnyTextn are equal, comparing without one "/" at their end
- none of AnyText1 .. AnyTextn starts with another of AnyText1 .. AnyTextn that does not end with "/", followed by "/"
- Zip is the tree of AnyText1 .. AnyTextn split at "/", where each name of the tree is the Segment with that name as fearlessProject.text(Desk, Segment), and each of AnyText1 .. AnyTextn that ends with "/" is a Zip

Implementation notes:
A unit of a Segment is a byte on Linux and on macOS, and a 16 bit unit on Windows.
For a File of a folder, Desk.time(File) is the modification time that the desk gives; Desk.time(Id) is the modification time that the desk gives for that folder.
2147483639 is the number of bytes of the longest array of Java.
The DeskPath of a Fearless project can go through a symbolic link, for example "/tmp" on macOS: Desk.at is undefined for that DeskPath, so that Fearless project is not well shaped. The manager refuses that path when the Fearless project is registered. The code that tests the shape rules reads only the folder at the end of the path, and does not refuse it: this difference is known and stays.
The time of an entry of a zip file is the time that the zip file stores with no time zone, read as UTC. A zip file can also store other times for an entry: no rule reads them.
For a File of a Zip, Desk.time(File) is the Desk.time of the File of a folder that holds that Zip.
